    {
      "caption": "Similarity: lengths, areas and volumes",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "Two similar rectangles \u2014 every length on the big one is twice the small one, so k equals two. Areas scale by k squared: four times. Volumes would scale by k cubed: eight times. Check which ratio you need before you multiply.",
